2. Scope and Prior-Art Boundary

External vibration sensing, acoustic correlation, wireless accelerometer networks, clamp-mounted sensors, and distributed acoustic sensing are established prior art [P]. Water Nerve claims no novelty in any of these mechanisms.

The research gap is the combination of: (i) retrofit clamp-on sensing with no plumbing modification, (ii) building-specific baseline learning under non-stationary usage, (iii) sequential detection with formal optimality guarantees and provable false-alarm control, (iv) energy-constrained duty-cycled acquisition with a designed wake-up comparator, (v) multi-stream fusion across a tree-structured plumbing network, and (vi) a documented link budget that ties Q_\ell^{\min} to sensor noise and mounting reproducibility.

Whether this combination is novel is a patent question and is not addressed here.

