5.1 Two hardware variants — mandatory

Proposition 5.1. [D]

A single AFE cannot serve both metal and plastic pipes without violating either the Nyquist criterion or the noise budget.

Proof. Metal pipes carry useful leak energy to 5 kHz; Nyquist requires f_s \geq 10 kHz, and a practical anti-alias filter at f_c = 5 kHz. Plastic pipes carry useful leak energy only below 800 Hz; sampling at f_s = 2 kHz is optimal for the noise budget but violates Nyquist for metal. Conversely, a 20 kHz sampler on PEX wastes 10× power and injects 5 kHz–10 kHz airborne interference directly into the band. \square

