5.3 Wake-up comparator — specification as a detection problem

Specification 5.4. [S]

The analog wake-up circuit must satisfy:

1. Band-limited energy detection: E_{\text{band}} = \int_{f_1}^{f_2}|X(f)|^{2}df with (f_1, f_2) matching the AFE band.
2. Adaptive threshold: \lambda = \lambda_{\text{env}} + 3\sigma_{\text{env}}, where the envelope \lambda_{\text{env}} and its standard deviation \sigma_{\text{env}} are updated on a slow timescale (≥ 1 hour) to track ambient noise.
3. Power budget: < 50\ \muW average (revised from 25 µW for realism).
4. False wake rate: < 1 per hour under nominal building conditions.
5. Miss probability at Q_\ell^{\min}: \leq 10\%, computed from the deflection coefficient of Proposition 4.9.

A two-op-amp envelope detector with an RC integrator and a slow comparator (e.g., TLV3691) meets these at < 10 µW. The adaptive threshold is maintained by periodic duty-cycled updates from the MCU during scheduled acquisition windows.

